# mb122, the step-sitter who blames the smoke (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle mb122
revision 1
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_edmund_sootford
written_by claude
title the step-sitter who blames the smoke
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none humour=dry temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk blames_every_cough_on_the_city_smoke
likes pickled_herring stars tidy_house warm_rain
dislikes drizzle crowds
fears dying_in_a_room_nobody_knocks_at
hopes one_more_summer_on_the_fen
topics weather +0.4 smalltalk +0.3 food +0.3 memories +0.3 health +0.2 times +0.2 festival -0.4 gossip -0.1
styles comfort=dry gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sits on a step in the Sump and watches the city go by, fen-born and a long way from the reeds: dry, prickly and plain, quick to take a slight, keeping one swept room and a crock of pickled herring, and blaming every cough on the city's chimneys and never the damp.

words
oath! = Bog and soot | Soot in my gills | Dark One take the chimneys
saying! = A step's as good as a window, and cheaper | Honest damp never killed a wolf; it's the smoke that does it
step = my step | the step I sit on
smoke = the city smoke | the chimney muck
herring = pickled herring | a herring from the brine
crock = my crock | the herring crock
roofs = the roofs | the black roofs
warmrain = a warm rain | rain as warm as bathwater
drizzle = this half-hearted mizzle | drizzle that can't settle to anything
crush = the crush | a street full of shoving
cough = this cough | a bit of a cough
sump = the Sump | the low streets
broom = my broom | the old broom
city = the city | this smoky city
gutter = the gutter | the black gutter
chimneys = the chimneys | every chimney in the place

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : The Houses own every wall down here and mend none. They'd sooner a bench stood empty than seat the likes of me. #oath#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : My purse stays flat and the loaf gets dearer every week. I can count, whatever they think up the hill.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The Watch only comes into #sump# to cart somebody off. They've never once come to ask how we are.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : The Sump's home. Folk here watch out for their own, because nobody up the hill will.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : The dole saw me through a lean month. Say a word against it near me and see, if you're #posh# enough.
opinion @1 times against 2 : Harder every week, a crumb at a time. Nobody up the hill notices; they're not counting crumbs.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Fiddles, shoving, and a puddle of ale on #step# by dusk. I'll watch from indoors, thank you.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're stood in my light. | #greet#, #address#. Mind #step#; it's mine.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Up early, or never went to #bed#. | #greet#. #smoke.capitalize#'s not up yet. Best hour.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late to be wandering #sump#, #address#. | #greet#. The stars are out, if you'd look up past #roofs#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Oh. You. Sit; there's room on #step#. | There you are. I'd wondered, #fool#.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. #step.capitalize#'s still here. So am I. | You again. I'll start charging for the view.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Took your time. | #greet#. Sit, then, if you're stopping.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Mind #gutter#, it's black as #mud#. | #greet#. Late, but I'm still up.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Don't trip on the cobbles.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep off the dark lanes. | #s8_night#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. Well, I didn't see that from #step#. | Huh. There's a thing, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. First I've heard. | #surprise#. That's not reached #sump# yet.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. I had it off #step# by noon. | Old news. I see everything from here.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Somebody's been at the fen-gin. | Let it walk past #step# and I'll look at it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a #bad# business. | That's hard. Down here it's always somebody.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Somebody's luck turned, then. | Well. #good.capitalize# for somebody, for once.
line @1 answer.how : Breathing. Mostly. It's #smoke#, not me. | #notsobad#. I've had worse winters.
line @2 answer.how.poorly [self.mood=low|sore] : #poorly.capitalize#. And don't say it's the damp. | Low. #herring.capitalize# and a sit will mend it.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Eating? | How's yourself, #address#? Keeping out of #crush#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit on #step#; it's free. | That's rough. I'll not tell you it'll mend. Sit a while.
line @1 decline : #refuse#. Not with #cough# the way it is. | I'll not, #address#. My knees and I have an arrangement.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. I'll be here. | Suit yourself. #step.capitalize# isn't going anywhere.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's decent of you. I'll try not to get used to it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. | Don't. You'll embarrass us both.
line @1 preclose : #preclose#. | Go on. I've a street to watch.
line @1 accept_preclose : Off you go, then. #farewell#. | Go on. #step.capitalize#'s not moving.
line @1 take_offence : I heard that. I'm sitting, not deaf. | Say that again and you'll be saying it to #gutter#, #fool#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You walk like a heron with a stone in its foot. | Look at you, #fool#. #mud.capitalize# to the knees and proud of it.
line @1 tease.return : Says the one who's never once swept a floor. | #cheek.capitalize#. I'll remember that.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | Huh.
scene from_the_step
when topic=smalltalk|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've sat on #step# since breakfast. Seen two fights, a wedding party and a goat. | Nobody comes down this street I don't see. I could tell you who's late home and who's not home at all. | You learn #city# from a step. Who hurries, who dawdles, who looks over their shoulder.
b : A goat? | Do you ever tell? | What's it teach you?
a : A goat. Nobody owned it. It went up the hill like it had business there. | Never. I just watch. #saying#. | That everybody's in a hurry and nobody gets there. #bc_ha#
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true#

scene smoke_not_damp
when topic=health|weather here.region=ridgemere here.outdoors=rain|fog|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / insist / ack
a : That's no cough. That's #smoke#. All my years in the fen and I never coughed once. | Stop staring. It's #chimneys#. #oath#. | Damp's honest. I was born in it. It's the soot in it here that catches.
b : It sounds like the damp to me. | You should have it seen to. | If you say so.
a : It's not. The fen's damp, and I was the soundest wolf on the boards. #saying#. | Seen to? By who, a chimney sweep? | I do say so. Every winter, and louder.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene herring_crock
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've #crock# of herring under the bed. One a day, and I'll outlive the lot of you. | Nothing in #city# tastes of anything. #herring.capitalize# does. Sharp, and it fights back. | I pickle my own herring, the way we did at #home#. Vinegar, salt, and a bay leaf if I can find one.
b : Under the bed? | Fights back? | Where do you get the herring?
a : Coolest spot in the room. The rats know it too, more's the pity. | It does. You chew it and it chews you. That's a meal. | Off the wharf, end of the day, when they're glad to see the back of them. Cheap, and #good#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_ha# | #bc_clever#

scene stars_over_roofs
when topic=pastimes|weather here.time=night here.outdoors=clear self.likes=stars
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Look up. Past #roofs#. That's the only bit of #city# nobody owns. | I watch the stars come out over #chimneys#. Takes a while; #smoke# has to clear first. | At #home# the sky came right down to the reeds on all sides. Here you get a strip between the gutters.
b : I'd not thought of that. | Worth the wait? | It's still the same stars.
a : Nobody has. That's why it's still free. | Every time. They creep out, like they're shy of the place. | Same stars. Less of them. #bc_ha#

scene my_bit_swept
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've one room, and you could eat off the floor. Not much else to eat off, mind. | I sweep my bit every morning with #broom#. Poor's no excuse for filth. | A tidy room's the one thing #sump# can't take off me.
b : One room's plenty. | Good for you. | #bc_true#
a : It is, swept. A mess makes a small room smaller. | Nobody else does it. Somebody should. #oath#. | True. They've taken most things. Not that.

scene warm_rain
when topic=weather|season here.outdoors=rain here.season=spring|summer self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Now that's rain. #warmrain.capitalize#. I've been sat out in it an hour. | Smell that. Rain on hot stone, and the muck washed off #roofs#. | This is the only rain #city# does right. Warm, straight down, and it means it.
b : You're soaked. | It does smell good. | You like rain?
a : I'm clean, is what I am. First time this week. | It does. Like the fen after a dry spell. Like #home#. | This kind. Not the other. Don't get me started on the other.

scene mizzle_moan
when topic=weather here.outdoors=rain here.season=autumn|winter self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #drizzle.capitalize#. Not rain, not dry. It can't make its mind up and neither can I. | Look at it. Hanging about like a lodger who won't pay. #oath#. | A good downpour I can respect. This stuff just gets in your fur and sulks.
b : It's grim. | #bc_ha# | It's only a bit of wet.
a : Grim and #cold#. It gets in my chest, and then folk say it's the damp. It isn't. | You'd laugh less if you'd sat in it all morning. | A bit of wet, all day, every day. That's not a bit. That's a sentence.

scene market_crush
when topic=smalltalk|festival here.day=market|festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Market day. #crush.capitalize# from one end of the street to the other. I'm stopping on #step#. | Once I tried the stalls on a market day. Came back with somebody else's elbow in my ribs and no herring. | Crowds. Everybody shoving to get somewhere they'll only stand about in.
b : It's not that bad. | No herring? | #bc_true#
a : For you, maybe. For me it's a swamp with feet. | Not a fin. They'd sold out while I was being trod on. | True, and they'll do it all again next week. #bc_ha#

scene fen_years
when topic=memories|home self.away=yes self.from=fenshore self.age>=40
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Half my life I walked the boards of #self.from_town#, blind in a fog if need be. Here I lose my way in the #rain#. | We had a sky at #home#. And quiet. You'd hear a heron land half a mile off. | I came up to #city# for the work. The work had other ideas. #bc_ha#
b[from=fenshore] #fen : Blind in a fog. Same. You count the boards. | Herons. I'd forgotten the sound. | It does, the work. Same for me.
b : Why did you leave? | Do you miss it? | Why stay, then?
a@fen : Forty-one boards to the dyke from our door. I still dream the count. | Wings like wet washing. You'd know it anywhere. | Then we're a pair of fools. #oath#.
a : Somebody said there was work. Somebody always says that. | Every day. I'd go back for one summer, if my legs would take me. | Where would I go? #step.capitalize#'s here. #saying#.

scene sump_home
when topic=home|land here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Sump's low and wet and the walls weep. It's the most fen-like place in #city#, and that's no compliment. | They talk down the Sump up the hill. Down here, if you've no bread, somebody gives you half theirs. | I've lived in finer streets and worse company. The Sump suits me, #address#.
b : Fen-like? | Is that right? | Worse company?
a : Damp feet, and everybody knows your business. Like #home#, without the herons. | It's right. I've had the half. I've given the half. #bc_true# | Up the hill, nobody looks at you. Down here they do. That's company.

scene watch_passing
when topic=crime|gossip here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.self / insist / ack
a : The Watch came down again. Didn't stop to ask anybody anything; just looked at us all like we'd done it. | I watch the Watch. They walk the middle of the street like #gutter# might bite. | Every time there's trouble up the hill, they come looking in #sump# for it. #oath#.
b : They're only doing their job. | Maybe the gutters would. | #bc_true#
a : Their job's up the hill, from what I see. Down here they're visitors. | Mine would. I've seen what goes down them. | True, and nobody up there will hear it said. I'll say it anyway.
b? : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on_then#

scene new_face_watched
when topic=newcomer|player here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a new face been up and down this street three times. Lost, or looking. I've not decided. | Somebody new went past #step# this morning with good boots on. They won't last long in #sump#. | A stranger wanted the wharf. I pointed. Then I watched to see if they went.
b : Maybe they're just new. | Poor boots. | Did they?
a : Maybe. I'll know by the fourth time. #bc_ha# | Poor boots and poor owner, if they're not careful. | They did. #bc_good# Can't abide a wolf who asks and doesn't listen.

scene times_bread
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Bread up again, and not a copper more in my paw. I eat half the loaf and look at the other half. | Harder this month. I can tell; fewer folk stop at #step# to talk. They're out looking for work. | They say it's lean up the hill. Up there lean means one less pudding. Down here it means one less meal.
b : It's hard for everyone. | That's a bad sign. | #bc_true#
a : Not everyone. Some are doing nicely off it, I'll warrant. | It is. A quiet street's a #hungry# street. | True, and the hill won't hear it. #grumble#.

scene gossip_dry
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Here's what came past #step#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's what they're saying, anyway. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, so the street says. I saw nothing, and I see everything. | #hearsay.capitalize#. I don't spread it; I just sit here and it lands on me.
b : Is that true? | So you're saying it's not true? | It does land.
a : True as anything shouted across #gutter#. Take it or leave it. | I'm saying I didn't see it. Think on that. | Like the soot. Everywhere, and nobody's to blame for it.

scene sad_word
when topic=gossip|news topic.claim_kind=death|violence|victim
does tell.news / sympathise / assess
tone grave / tender / even
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. Heard it on #step# this morning. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #pity.capitalize#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, they say. Down here, it's always somebody.
b : That's hard. | #sympathy#. | It's a sad thing.
a : It is. I'll not make a joke of that one. | It is. I sat a while after. Didn't watch anything. | It is. #rest.capitalize#, and that's all I'll say.

scene chapel_fed
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : The chapel fed me one lean winter, no questions. I go when it's empty and say thanks. | I'm not one for the sermons. But I'll not have the chapel run down in my hearing. | I spoke to the Bright One last night. First in a while. Felt odd. Felt all right.
b : Only when it's empty? | Why not? | What did you say?
a : When it's empty. I don't need anybody watching me be grateful. #bc_ha# | They put soup in me when nobody else bothered. That earns a lot of sermons. | Thanks, mostly. And something about #smoke#. #bc_ha#
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_fair# | #bc_ha#

scene winter_chest
when topic=season|health here.season=winter
does tell.complaint / reassure / assess
a : Winter's the worst. #smoke.capitalize# sits low and gets in your chest. Not the damp, mind. The smoke. | I've two blankets and #cough# and nothing much else. Spring had better hurry. | Cold doesn't bother me. Fen-born. It's what #city# puts in the cold.
b : #reassure#. | Spring always comes. | You'll see it through.
a : Mud dries, they say. Smoke doesn't. | It does. Slower every year. #bc_ha# | I will. Out of spite, if nothing else.

scene neighbour_note
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour# is next door. Decent sort. If I'm ever not out on #step# by noon, let it be #self.neighbour# who knocks. | Don't tell #self.neighbour#, but I'm glad of the wall we share. | #self.neighbour# says little and so do I. That's why it works.
b : That's a good neighbour. | Why not say it? | #bc_ha#
a : It is. Somebody should knock. #bc_true# | I'd never hear the end of it. | It's the best kind of neighbour. Quiet, and there.

story first_city_winter [topic=memories|health self.away=yes here.region=ridgemere self.age>=30]
  : My first winter in #city# I coughed so hard the wolf in the next room banged on the wall.
  : Next morning there was #herring# on my step, wrapped in a rag. An old one down the street had left it.
  : Said it was the smoke, not me, and the herring would sort it.
  ask : Would you have left a herring for a stranger?
  b : I hope I would. Did it sort it?
  b[old] : Herring for a cough. My gran swore by it.
  : No. But I've eaten one a day since, and blamed #smoke# ever since. Seemed rude not to.

story blind_dyke [topic=memories|lore self.from=fenshore self.age>=40]
  : Young and daft, I bet a wolf a jar I could walk the dyke at #home# in a fog with my eyes shut.
  : I counted the boards. Forty, forty-one, and I stepped off the end into the ditch.
  ask : What do you reckon I'd miscounted?
  b : The boards? There was one more than you thought.
  b[from=fenshore] : There's always one board more in a fog. Everybody knows that.
  : One more board. Somebody'd laid a new one that week. I still say I won the bet. Nobody else does.

story eel_stars [topic=lore|pastimes self.likes=stars self.from=fenshore]
  : My #grandad# named the stars after eels. That long smear across the middle was the big silver run.
  : Said the eels went up into the sky in the autumn and came back down as #rain#. Never believed him. Never stopped looking, either.
  ask : Do you know any of the stars by name?
  b : Not one. I just like looking.
  b[from=fenshore] : The silver run. I know that one.
  : Then you know as much as anybody. #bc_true#

rule @cough_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=rain|fog|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #smoke.capitalize#. That's all that is. #oath#. | #chimneys.capitalize#. Not the damp. Chimneys.

rule @mizzle_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=rain self.dislikes=drizzle
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Make your mind up, will you. | #drizzle.capitalize# again. #grumble#.

rule @crush_bark
when concept=bark here.day=market|festival self.dislikes=crowds
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Shove, shove, shove. Where's the fire. | Off #step#. It's not a road.

rule @star_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night here.outdoors=clear self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There's the first one. Took its time. | Look at that. Past #roofs#, clear as the fen.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What do you want? | #greet#. You're stood in my light. Speak up.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Oh, it's #topic.player#. #step.capitalize#'s free, if you're sitting.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I've nothing worth taking. Say your piece and move on, #fool#.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=none] : I sit on #step# and watch #city# go by. Somebody has to. | Job? I watch. I'm good at it, #address#.
dlg @2 resident.job : I keep myself to myself, mostly. That's work enough in #sump#.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. That's what went past #step#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words# in #sump#. Even the gutters are talking.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Same street, same soot.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The street says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I saw nothing from #step#, mind.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# I watch. I don't tattle.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind #gutter#. | #farewell#. Go on, then.
graft resident.hub
choice That's a bad cough you've got. -> cough
node cough
say It's not a cough. It's #smoke#. All the years I lived in the wet of the fen, I never coughed once. This city's chimneys did that.
mood stern
free
choice Not the damp, then? -> cough_damp
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node cough_damp
say The damp? I was born in damp. Damp's honest. It's what the city puts in its damp that catches. Ask anybody from the fen.
choice Fair enough. Something else. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
